{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fix pushed for review: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1479 (change 1479).\n\nAdded a `make venv` target that provisions .venv with `uv venv --python <pinned>` and FAILS\nloudly (naming the version and the `uv python install` remedy) rather than falling back to\nambient python3. `make worktree` now delegates to it before the already-correct `make install`.\n\nThe version is single-sourced in `.github/python-version.txt` (3.12), the same discipline as\n`.github/git-version-floor.txt`. `tests/unit/test_worktree_python_pin.py` holds it to the CI\nmatrix in _build-and-test.yml AND to the actions/setup-python pins, so dropping 3.12 from CI\nreddens a test instead of silently leaving fresh venvs on an untested rev.\n\nVerified end-to-end: `make venv` in a scratch tree produced Python 3.12.13 while this host's\nambient python3 is 3.14.6.\n\nRe-check of the two failures this bug was found through, on Python 3.12.13 (the last AC):\n  - tests/unit/grounding/test_coverage_reconstruction.py::test_full_backend_account_is_present\n    -> PASSES. It was an artifact of the untested interpreter. No ticket needed.\n  - tests/unit/metrics/test_jscpd_dup_heldout.py::test_live_clone\n    -> STILL FAILS (assert 0 >= 1) with jscpd 5.0.14 installed. Genuinely unrelated to the\n       Python rev, so filed as a real bug: 4bf4 (exultant-pinelike-prairiedog), linked\n       discovered_from this ticket.\n\nDocs updated: docs/local-dev-env.md gained a 'provision the venv on the Python CI tests'\nprerequisite section mirroring the Git-floor one, and AGENTS.md's Codex bootstrap line now says\n`make venv` instead of `python3 -m venv .venv`."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786096002246471001,"uuid":"07ffad7f-cb18-4707-a1f8-96bf1f448ed8"}